<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<archimate:model xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:archimate="http://www.archimatetool.com/archimate" name="View architecture" id="id-b4f0f222463b5c0b8be1432bc16802f6" version="5.0.0">
  <folder name="Strategy" id="id-2ba35f8b13c65c01a1ba3070126f8cf5" type="strategy"/>
  <folder name="Business" id="id-cad1d779be9055b0930f75879cf71278" type="business">
    <folder name="Actors" id="id-c0ae2a3753565dd88826ddd6a618d72f">
      <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Architect" id="id-177372ec9dd352829fa2ccb3ba06432f">
        <documentation>Uses the View scripts in Archi: generates and re-lays out views with the dialog or an entry script, and reports a view that looks wrong.</documentation>
        <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Developer" id="id-ff6e08d3272952088feb43dd273b8c8a">
        <documentation>Owns the View subsystem: agrees on behaviour, checks results in Archi (dialog, readability, baseline), approves and commits.</documentation>
        <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="AI coding agent" id="id-9d0113fc3d495535b63e6e545fbf131e">
        <documentation>A coding agent (Claude Code, Copilot) that follows AGENTS.md, Scripts/View/AGENTS.md and the skills: plans, builds, runs the Node checks and Archi's command line, writes the docs. Asks only for decisions, approvals and checks only the developer can do.</documentation>
        <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="Processes" id="id-c4939252777259d5ad0a0b28b2571995">
      <folder name="Generate views" id="id-665b7955ce90557fa4e7300d86e893f1">
        <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Generate a view with the dialog" id="id-d992e94509ba52e8bef664ccaf15fedb">
          <documentation>The architect selects concepts, views or folders, opens the Generate View dialog, picks a preset or edits the settings while the counts show what the view will hold, and runs an action: New view, One view each, Expand view or Layout only.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Generate a view with an entry script" id="id-3c88c9041dc45af59166b038d1e5138f">
          <documentation>The architect runs an entry script on the selection: the base preset with fixed overrides, the session, or a preset named by the script's file name. No dialog.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Manage presets" id="id-2d3c1c3b4f5c5cae96fef4321952f2ed">
          <documentation>The architect saves, renames and deletes presets in the dialog's preset row; presets are shared through the repo, the session stays local.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Generate GGM views" id="id-b445044a297e50238385ffcb115df13a">
          <documentation>The architect generates the views of the GGM data objects and GEMMA business objects (Scripts/GEMMA/GGM), with presets in presets/GEMMA/GGM.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
      </folder>
      <folder name="Develop a View change" id="id-e996b3484c365dac86f51d34d7fbe647">
        <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Design" id="id-a053c85ad93f57069ee6446579a68e47">
          <documentation>Agree on the behaviour with the developer; a change of more than one step gets a plan in plan/ (repo rule 8).</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Agree on the behaviour" id="id-1634b4376d2954a9a8495b301d639340">
          <documentation>Developer and agent agree on the behaviour or solution before code changes (Scripts/View/AGENTS.md § Order of change, step 1). Reads SPEC, ARCHITECTURE and the reference doc of the subject.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Write a plan" id="id-55b23d1474fd54bf87f56a64c5066677">
          <documentation>Steps with dependencies and status, the doc sections it builds on, the test data and a dated step log, saved as plan/&lt;title>.md.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Build" id="id-a816bef21bb05b1787dc53cc482519d3">
          <documentation>Registry first: a new option or value goes into defs.js (defaults, labels, tooltips, capability), then the pipeline, adapter, writer or dialog (ARCHITECTURE § Extension recipes).</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Change the registry" id="id-bd6c83b5ac645eee8cd0b73c43f8e05b">
          <documentation>Add or change an option, value, algorithm, action or condition list in defs.js; DEFAULT_PRESET.params holds every params key, or validatePreset drops it (Scripts/View/AGENTS.md rule 9).</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Change pipeline, adapter, writer or dialog" id="id-f79ded61cb6e548487ae12da533a3ce1">
          <documentation>Change the modules the recipe names, in its order; hard rules of Scripts/View/AGENTS.md apply (no post-layout scaling, adapters never touch a view, one write path, determinism).</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Migrate the preset shape" id="id-7030316550535c27b8cc661f6a9b8f6d">
          <documentation>A changed preset shape raises schemaVersion and gets a one-shot migration in tools/ that rewrites every preset and the session (repo rule 3: no compat shim).</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Test" id="id-4a50986ad76053b497248c360d32eb79">
          <documentation>The test levels from cheap to Archi; a step is done when its levels pass. Checks only the developer can do in Archi stay open in the plan until confirmed.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Run the Node checks" id="id-89f2cdfc20315d7caa8824ce7cc204db">
          <documentation>Typecheck, unit, consistency, write-plan, layout and rule checks in Node, without Archi.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Run the Archi baseline" id="id-5e5e6e25d05e52a891cc08c30e1e9465">
          <documentation>Skill view-baseline: run_baseline.ajs writes the 12-run matrix into a copy of the test model through Archi's command line; compare-views.js, console_checks.js and the rendering checks judge it.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Check in Archi" id="id-dcb82fdc926d50b38e1d5e625ce6c849">
          <documentation>What needs a person: the SWT dialog (controls, greying, counts while editing) and whether a view reads well.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Rebuild the test model" id="id-3fd888f54abf5b978f0aee1b72774bda">
          <documentation>build_test_model.ajs rebuilds test/model/view-test.archimate; every id changes, so run_baseline.ajs and every expected file follow in the same commit.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Approve" id="id-db6f797cc3b150ff9542c7531e39453f">
          <documentation>The developer checks the result in Archi and approves. Until then no change to SPEC, docs/reference, ARCHITECTURE or the generated tables (Scripts/View/AGENTS.md § Order of change).</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Document" id="id-e148f48b152859619ac0d077f312f5b7">
          <documentation>After approval: behaviour in SPEC (detail in docs/reference), decision and realisation in ARCHITECTURE under its subject, then the generated tables; docs and code in one commit.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
      </folder>
      <folder name="Version and commit" id="id-5e9e4aac54845a6c98c84cbede533710">
        <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Rewrite the expected files" id="id-58905b4a99e65683a34f55728ce90973">
          <documentation>A meant change of write plans, layouts, rule violations or warnings: the tool's --write rewrites its file in test/expected/, committed with the change. A local Graphviz upgrade also changes GRAPHVIZ_VERSION in check.yml.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Commit" id="id-22af7c03a93f5327b4625caedf141a04">
          <documentation>Docs and code in one commit; typecheck at exit 0 (repo rule 5); no co-author line and no AI mention (repo rule 4); renames update every site, no compat shim (repo rule 3).</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Push" id="id-fb55bfa953955e338bc1067364ddfd20">
          <documentation>Push the branch; CI runs on every push and pull request.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
      </folder>
      <folder name="Diagnose a reported view" id="id-afa4e4b9bd465be9a9538463ccd03101">
        <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Report a view that looks wrong" id="id-3e96d99443295ac68b1e33994d744f63">
          <documentation>The architect names the view and the preset that gave it.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Find model, preset and session" id="id-87c9d86f9c0a51c9a2869ba6d3bdd92a">
          <documentation>Find the model file (with coArchi the saved working copy), the preset and what actually ran: preset_diff.js against the session.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Reproduce in the Node harness" id="id-1a0d7106db585264aeee7170722ae220">
          <documentation>view_harness.js runs the run's own plan() on the view from the model file: object set, nesting, layout graph, engine, write plan.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Find the cause" id="id-7326fe3a0cf65de0a0b2f5f0d0632733">
          <documentation>Locate the cause in the pipeline, adapter or engine options; measure gaps, overlaps and line lengths from the model file and the console log.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Log the case" id="id-83dbf117e18e5ecd829d842f1d95f30b">
          <documentation>Record view, preset, finding, cause, change and status in docs/test-cases.md; a fix enters the development cycle.</documentation>
          <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
        </element>
      </folder>
      <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Generate views" id="id-79f443d9e8b352f0b0545d78ccaba51e">
        <documentation>The architect generates and re-lays out views with the View scripts: with the dialog, with an entry script, or with the GGM scripts, and keeps the presets.</documentation>
        <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Develop a View change" id="id-c5ab1fd5cc9353bbbd10a12f765d7637">
        <documentation>The development cycle of Scripts/View/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md § Development and testing: Design → Build → Test → Approve → Document, then version and commit.</documentation>
        <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Version and commit" id="id-3b34e3881040570ca4c8e7b7c7fd1e08">
        <documentation>Bring expected files, docs and code together in one commit, push, and let CI check the clean clone.</documentation>
        <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Diagnose a reported view" id="id-5b1dee3a82e35270a4d941b12ea90d95">
        <documentation>Skill view-testing: a generated or laid-out view looks wrong; find the model, preset and session, reproduce in Node, find the cause, log the case.</documentation>
        <property key="view-architecture export date" value="2026-11-03T16:31:01.749Z"/>
      </element>
    </folder>
